    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 462,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 375,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66330,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 472,
        "headingId": 375,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours occurring in patients with VHL include CNS and retinal haemangioblastomas, inner ear endolymphatic sac tumours, renal cell carcinoma, pancreatic serous cystadenoma and neuroendocrine tumours (NETs), phaeochromocytoma and paraganglioma, and genital tract papillary cystadenomas {29083737}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-23T16:48:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 463,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 376,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66331,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 472,
        "headingId": 376,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The age of onset is most commonly 18&ndash;30&nbsp;years (average: 26&nbsp;years) but ranges from 5 to 65&nbsp;years. Females and males are equally affected {25905347}. The clinical symptoms depend on the location and size of the tumours. Haemangioblastomas in the CNS cause headache, vomiting, sensory or motor deficits, and ataxia; haemangioblastomas in the retina may cause vision loss. Phaeochromocytomas may be asymptomatic or may cause symptoms related to excess of catecholamines, including headaches, panic attacks, excessive sweating, and elevated blood pressure. Endolymphatic sac tumours in the inner ear may cause tinnitus, vertigo, or hearing loss. Papillary cystadenomas of the broad ligament are usually asymptomatic. The diagnosis is usually made on the basis of laboratory and radiological findings. Family history is important for unravelling the hereditary nature of the disease {29083737}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-23T16:48:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 464,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 377,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66332,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 472,
        "headingId": 377,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The estimated prevalence in the USA is 1&nbsp;case per 30&nbsp;000&ndash;50&nbsp;000&nbsp;births {20301636}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-23T16:48:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 465,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 378,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66333,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 472,
        "headingId": 378,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>VHL is caused by germline mutations in the <em>VHL</em> tumour suppressor gene, located on chromosome 3p25.3.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-23T16:48:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 466,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 379,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66334,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 472,
        "headingId": 379,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Abnormal or absent VHL protein results in uninhibited upregulation of HIF (a protein responsible for cellular oxygen regulation) and multiple downstream growth factors and subsequently leads to the formation of cysts and angiomatous tumours {16818478; 29083737}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-23T16:48:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 473,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 386,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66335,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 472,
        "headingId": 386,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The macroscopic appearance is not specific.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-23T16:48:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 467,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 380,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66336,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 472,
        "headingId": 380,
        "headingText": "<p>Tumours can be either benign (haemangioblastoma, phaeochromocytoma, endolymphatic sac tumours) or malignant (renal cell carcinoma, NETs). Cysts are also common and occur in the kidneys, pancreas, and genital tract. In the genital tract, papillary cystadenoma may occur, more commonly in the epididymis than in the broad ligament or the mesosalpinx (see <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/chaptercontent/34/213\" target=\"_blank\">section </a><em>Papillary cystadenoma</em>). Bilaterality is considered pathognomonic {27241108}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-10T14:11:04"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 468,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 381,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66337,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 472,
        "headingId": 381,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not clinically relevant</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-23T16:48:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 469,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 382,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66338,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 472,
        "headingId": 382,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The identification of germline <em>VHL</em> mutations is necessary for definitive diagnosis or to confirm a clinically suspected case.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-23T16:48:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 472,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 385,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66339,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 472,
        "headingId": 385,
        "headingText": "<p><em>Essential:</em> papillary cystadenoma is very rare outside the setting of VHL&nbsp;&ndash; bilaterality is essentially pathognomonic; tumours and cysts at early age {27241108}; confirmation of diagnosis by germline mutation analysis.</p>\r\n<p>See <a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/34/472/13061\" target=\"_blank\">#13061</a>Box&nbsp;<a style=\"cursor:pointer\" href=\"/attachment/34/472/13061\" target=\"_blank\">#13061</a>.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-07-10T14:11:23"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 470,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 383,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66340,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 472,
        "headingId": 383,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Malignant tumours are staged according to the site-specific TNM system.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-23T16:48:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 471,
    "bookid": 34,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 384,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 66341,
        "bookId": 34,
        "chapterId": 472,
        "headingId": 384,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Prognosis is related to the various diseases and their site-specific complications.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2020-06-23T16:48:38"
      }
    ],
